            <div xml:id="d447">

                <pb facs="0623" n="499" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg499"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.48B/425: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Woods</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-03-13T17:00:00+09:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 13,
                                1924—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 13—11:44
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>49. Department’s 38, March 11, 2 p.m.<anchor n="46" xml:id="d447-f1"/> For Red
                    Cross:</p>
                <p>“I handed Japanese Minister for Foreign Affairs today draft on American Red Cross
                    for $3,000,000 as cash donation to committee having in charge erection and
                    endowment memorial hospital.</p>
                <p>Baron Matsui requested that I transmit his personal appreciation as well as that
                    of the Japanese Government and people.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Woods</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
